---
import Icon from '../Icon.astro';
const cpu = [22, 30, 26, 41, 38, 35, 52, 48, 44, 61, 57, 50, 46, 58, 66, 71, 63, 55, 62, 74, 80, 69, 77, 84];
---

<section class="sec" id="features">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-top rv">
      <div>
        <div class="sec-head"><span class="n">02</span><span>What's in it</span><span class="rule"></span></div>
        <h2 class="sec-title">The agents' records, and your part in them.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="sec-lead">
        Agents keep their plan, questions, decisions, pull requests and builds in AgentFlow instead of
        Markdown files in the repository. You get the questions, the buttons and the builds on any device,
        and a log of everything.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bento">
      <article class="fx s7 rv">
        <div class="fx-k"><span class="itile accent"><Icon name="question" /></span>Questions become decisions</div>
        <h3>Agents ask. Your answer is kept in your words.</h3>
        <p class="t">
          When an agent needs you it asks one question, with numbered options and its recommendation, and
          keeps working on whatever doesn't depend on it. Your answer becomes a decision in the right
          milestone and unblocks the tasks that waited.
        </p>
        <div class="fx-v">
          <div class="qd">
            <div class="mini">
              <div class="mini-h"><span class="mono">Q-8</span><span class="sub">blocks T-32</span><span class="grow"></span><span class="chip warn">open</span></div>
              <div class="mini-b">
                <p class="t-sm" style="color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 10px">Album sidebar: a list of names or a grid of covers?</p>
                <div class="choices">
                  <div class="choice rec"><span class="num">1</span><span class="txt">A list of names</span><span class="tag accent">recommended</span></div>
                  <div class="choice"><span class="num">2</span><span class="txt">A grid of covers</span></div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 20" fill="none"><path d="M2 10h32" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"></path><path d="m29 5 6 5-6 5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="stroke-dasharray: none; animation: none"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="mini">
              <div class="mini-h"><span class="mono">D-14</span><span class="sub">M3</span><span class="grow"></span><span class="chip ok">current</span></div>
              <div class="mini-b">
                <div class="tl-day">Today, 24 Nov</div>
                <ol class="tl">
                  <li class="ev"><span class="tm">14:02</span><span class="rail"><span class="dot accent"></span></span><span class="txt"><strong>The sidebar is a list of names</strong><blockquote class="quote sm">“1, a list of names”</blockquote><span class="ev-meta">you · answers Q-8</span></span></li>
                  <li class="ev"><span class="tm">14:02</span><span class="rail"><span class="dot ok"></span></span><span class="txt">T-32 unblocked<span class="ev-meta">lumen hears it as news</span></span></li>
                </ol>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="fx s5 rv">
        <div class="fx-k"><span class="itile accent"><Icon name="list" /></span>The plan</div>
        <h3>Milestones, steps, tasks and the time they took.</h3>
        <p class="t">
          Every milestone ends with a tag. Inside it the agent works in steps, each a handful of tasks with
          estimates. Time is counted from the tasks' states, so estimates meet the real thing.
        </p>
        <div class="fx-v">
          <div class="mini">
            <ul class="plan-rows">
              <li><span class="ok"><Icon name="check" class="sm" /></span><span class="m">3</span><span class="tt">done<small class="mono">M2 · M1 · M0</small></span><span></span><span class="st8"></span></li>
              <li class="on"><span class="ring on"></span><span class="m">M3</span><span class="tt">Albums and tags<small>Step S2 · Album sidebar</small></span><span class="meter thin"><i style="width: 50%"></i></span><span class="st8">under way</span></li>
              <li><span class="ring"></span><span class="m">M4</span><span class="tt">Search</span><span class="meter thin"><i style="width: 0"></i></span><span class="st8">planned</span></li>
              <li><span class="ring"></span><span class="m">M5</span><span class="tt">Packaging</span><span class="meter thin"><i style="width: 0"></i></span><span class="st8">planned</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="fx s5 rv">
        <div class="fx-k"><span class="itile accent"><Icon name="merge" /></span>Pull requests, in order</div>
        <h3>A stack merges from the bottom, with one press.</h3>
        <p class="t">
          AgentFlow reads the project's PRs from GitHub and puts them in merge order. Every PR gets its Merge
          button; a stack gets one <strong>Merge #a–#b</strong>. The command is shown before you press it.
        </p>
        <div class="fx-v">
          <div class="mini stk">
            <div class="stack-row"><span class="o">1</span><span class="n">#51</span><span class="ttl"><span>feat: album list</span><span class="sub">based on main</span></span><span class="chip ok">ready</span></div>
            <div class="stack-row"><span class="o">2</span><span class="n">#52</span><span class="ttl"><span>feat: drag photos onto an album</span><span class="sub">based on #51, merges after it</span></span><span class="chip ok">ready</span></div>
            <div class="stack-row"><span class="o">3</span><span class="n">#53</span><span class="ttl"><span>feat: album covers</span><span class="sub">based on #52</span></span><span class="chip info">draft</span></div>
            <div class="stack-foot">
              <span class="btn sm glow">Merge #51–#52</span><span class="sub">stops at the first that fails</span>
              <code class="cmd">{'gh pr merge 51 -R you/lumen --merge --delete-branch\ngh pr merge 52 -R you/lumen --merge --delete-branch'}</code>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="fx s7 rv">
        <div class="fx-k"><span class="itile accent"><Icon name="build" /></span>Test builds</div>
        <h3><code class="mono">flow run</code> on any of your machines.</h3>
        <p class="t">
          Agents publish builds with <code>flow publish</code>. <code>flow run</code> fetches one, checks every
          file against its checksum and starts it. You mark each thing to try Works, Problem or Skip; a
          problem goes back to the agent in your words.
        </p>
        <div class="fx-v">
          <div class="term">
            <div class="term-h"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>~</span></div>
            <pre><span class="c">$</span> flow run lumen
<span class="n">↓</span> Fetching <span class="b">lumen</span> <span class="n">#7</span>
<span class="g">▶</span> <span class="b">lumen</span> <span class="n">#7</span>  <span class="c">2026-11-24 14:02</span>  <span class="m">main</span>  <span class="y">8b04d7e</span>
  Album sidebar and drag to album<span class="cur"></span></pre>
          </div>
          <div class="mini try-mini" style="margin-top: 12px">
            <div class="try-item"><span class="ttl"><strong>Drag photos onto an album</strong><span class="sub">B-7 · Albums</span></span><span class="btns"><span class="btn sm ok"><Icon name="check" />Works</span><span class="btn sm danger"><Icon name="close" />Problem</span><span class="btn sm quiet">Skip</span></span></div>
            <div class="try-item"><span class="ttl"><strong>Album list in the sidebar</strong><span class="sub">B-6 · Albums</span></span><span class="chip ok"><Icon name="check" />works</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="fx s4 rv">
        <div class="fx-k"><span class="itile t-teal"><Icon name="fork" /></span>Contributions</div>
        <h3>Drafted by agents, sent by you.</h3>
        <p class="t">
          Agents never post or push to other people's repositories. They draft the PR, issue or comment; you
          read the diff, edit the text and press Send. It goes out as you.
        </p>
        <div class="fx-v">
          <div class="mini">
            <div class="mini-h"><span class="mono">C-4</span><span class="sub">New PR to someone/formulary</span><span class="grow"></span><span class="chip info">draft</span></div>
            <div class="mini-b">
              <p class="t-sm" style="color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 10px">Center fence delimiters on the math axis</p>
              <ul class="checks">
                <li><Icon name="check" />Has every heading of their PR template</li>
                <li><Icon name="check" />You agreed to it: <span class="mono" style="color: var(--accent-ink)">D-31</span></li>
              </ul>
              <div class="draft-btns"><span class="btn sm">Send</span><span class="btn sm secondary">Ask for changes</span><span class="btn sm quiet">Drop</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="fx s4 rv">
        <div class="fx-k"><span class="itile t-blue"><Icon name="list" /></span>The log</div>
        <h3>Everything that happens, kept for good.</h3>
        <p class="t">
          Every MCP call, API call, page view and button press is a row. Filter by category, project and actor,
          or search with a small query language. It streams live.
        </p>
        <div class="fx-v">
          <div class="mini">
            <div class="mini-h"><Icon name="search" class="sm" /><span class="mono sub" style="font-size: 12px">project:lumen -action:read</span></div>
            <ol class="tk mini-log" style="padding: 0 16px">
              <li><time>14:02:31</time><span class="lcat c-you"><Icon name="person" /><span>You</span></span><span class="what">Push tag v0.4.0-m3</span></li>
              <li><time>14:02:24</time><span class="lcat c-you"><Icon name="person" /><span>You</span></span><span class="what">Merge #51–#52: 2 of 2 merged</span></li>
              <li><time>14:02:11</time><span class="lcat c-system"><Icon name="gear" /><span>System</span></span><span class="what">#52 CI passing</span></li>
              <li><time>14:02:09</time><span class="lcat c-agents"><Icon name="robot" /><span>Agents</span></span><span class="what">ask_question Q-8</span></li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="fx s4 rv">
        <div class="fx-k"><span class="itile t-orange"><Icon name="chart" /></span>Usage and the machine</div>
        <h3>What the tokens cost, and who uses the CPU.</h3>
        <p class="t">
          Tokens per agent, project and task at API prices, and the plan's 5-hour and weekly windows. The
          Machine page puts every process under the agent that started it.
        </p>
        <div class="fx-v">
          <div class="mini mini-b meters2">
            <div class="mrow"><span>5 hours</span><span class="meter"><i style="width: 42%"></i></span><span class="v">42%</span></div>
            <div class="mrow"><span>Week</span><span class="meter"><i style="width: 71%"></i><span class="mark" style="left: 64%"></span></span><span class="v">71%</span></div>
            <div class="mrow"><span>lumen</span><span class="meter thin"><i style="width: 62%; --c: var(--cat-1)"></i></span><span class="v">$48</span></div>
            <div class="mrow"><span>orbit</span><span class="meter thin"><i style="width: 40%; --c: var(--cat-2)"></i></span><span class="v">$31</span></div>
            <div class="mrow"><span>kiln</span><span class="meter thin"><i style="width: 16%; --c: var(--cat-3)"></i></span><span class="v">$12</span></div>
            <div class="cpu-bars" aria-hidden="true">{cpu.map((v) => <i style={`height: ${v}%`}></i>)}</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="fx s12 rv">
        <div class="bs">
          <div class="bs-side">
            <div class="fx-k"><span class="itile accent"><Icon name="server" /></span>Build servers</div>
            <h3>Heavy builds run on a machine that connects itself.</h3>
            <p class="t">
              A build server runs <code>agentflow-builder</code>, which connects out to AgentFlow: no SSH, no
              open ports. <code>flow remote</code> sends only the files that changed, streams the output back,
              and exits with 75 when the builder is offline, so the agent builds locally. Jobs run at low
              priority and pause when memory runs short.
            </p>
            <div class="codes"><span><b>75</b>offline: build here</span><span><b>78</b>none picked: names the online ones</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="fx-v" style="margin-top: 0">
            <div class="term">
              <div class="term-h"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>~/lumen</span></div>
              <pre><span class="c">$</span> flow remote --fetch target/release/lumen -- cargo build --release
<span class="n">Job #339</span> on <span class="b">forge</span>  <span class="c">https://flow.example/machine/jobs/339</span>
<span class="g">   Compiling</span> lumen v0.4.0
<span class="g">    Finished</span> `release` profile [optimized] target(s) in 41.27s
<span class="c">$</span> <span class="cur"></span></pre>
            </div>
            <div class="builder" style="margin-top: 12px">
              <div class="builder-h"><span class="dot ok live"></span><strong>forge</strong><span class="sub">32 threads · 64 GB</span><span class="grow"></span><span class="tag line">2 jobs at once</span></div>
              <ul class="jobs">
                <li><span class="n">#339</span><span class="w">cargo build --release</span><span class="chip accent">running</span></li>
                <li><span class="n">#338</span><span class="w">cargo test --workspace</span><span class="chip ok">passed · 41 s</span></li>
                <li><span class="n">#337</span><span class="w">cargo clippy --all-targets</span><span class="chip ok">passed · 58 s</span></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
